# Check text out with LF everywhere, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which converts every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. Several files here are read byte-for-byte: the
# skill and the board page are compiled in with go:embed, and the skill's
# frontmatter parser expects "---\n". A Windows build from a default checkout
# embedded CRLF copies and refused to set up a project ("embedded skill is
# missing YAML frontmatter"). Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
